WEBVTT

00:13.470 --> 00:16.050
<b>Stop, boy! Where are you going?</b>

00:16.590 --> 00:19.760
<b>I... I need to see the Demon King.</b>

00:20.060 --> 00:21.980
<b>Could you please let me through?</b>

00:21.980 --> 00:25.650
<b>The Demon King has passed away.
I’m afraid you won’t be able to see him.</b>

00:27.980 --> 00:32.030
<b>Get out of here. The Demon King can’t rest
in peace if you cause a commotion.</b>

02:05.790 --> 02:11.330
<b>THE LAND OF DEMONS WITHOUT A DEMON KING</b>

02:08.540 --> 02:09.540
<b>Hello!</b>

02:09.830 --> 02:12.090
<b>Are you heading for the flower garden, too, Anoshu?</b>

02:12.090 --> 02:13.000
<b>Yeah.</b>

02:14.630 --> 02:17.010
<b>Leno, can I ask you something?</b>

02:17.010 --> 02:18.260
<b>What is it?</b>

02:18.260 --> 02:21.260
<b>If you change the rumors and lore
of a Spirit who’s already been born,</b>

02:21.260 --> 02:23.970
<b>can you turn her into a Spirit
of the same name?</b>

02:23.970 --> 02:27.100
<b>Huh? Hmm... I’m not sure.</b>

02:27.100 --> 02:32.230
<b>Since it’s the rumors and lore from when she’s
first born that make up a Spirit’s spiritual essence.</b>

02:33.020 --> 02:37.400
<b>In my case, that would be “the mother of all Spirits.”</b>

02:37.400 --> 02:40.860
<b>But if rumors spread that
“Leno isn’t the Spirits’ mother,”</b>

02:40.860 --> 02:43.410
<b>then it would mean that I’d cease to exist.</b>

02:43.410 --> 02:45.910
<b>So if there are conflicts between
the spiritual essence and the lore,</b>

02:45.910 --> 02:48.500
<b>it would just reduce the Spirit’s lifespan?</b>

02:48.500 --> 02:49.370
<b>Yes.</b>

02:49.370 --> 02:53.630
<b>As long as the rumors and lore remain,
Spirits generally don’t get wiped out,</b>

02:53.630 --> 02:56.130
<b>but since we don’t get reincarnated
like demons and humans,</b>

02:56.420 --> 02:59.720
<b>we would never become a completely different Spirit.</b>

03:00.010 --> 03:03.090
<b><i>Avos Dilhevia’s root is “the Demon King of Tyranny”.</i></b>

03:03.090 --> 03:06.430
<b><i>I thought if I could change that,</i>
<i>it would take care of everything.</i></b>

03:06.430 --> 03:08.100
<b><i>But I guess it’s not that easy.</i></b>

03:08.100 --> 03:09.140
<b>But...</b>

03:09.430 --> 03:12.730
<b>If the rumors that were created
later match the Spirit,</b>

03:12.730 --> 03:14.270
<b>they could have some sway.</b>

03:14.770 --> 03:16.610
<b>For example,
these tear-flowers.</b>

03:16.610 --> 03:20.400
<b>A rumor that my tears spawn
Spirit children was created,</b>

03:20.400 --> 03:23.450
<b>and since it doesn’t contradict my lore
as the Great Spirit Mother,</b>

03:23.450 --> 03:26.410
<b>it’s given me that very power.</b>

03:27.240 --> 03:28.490
<b>I see.</b>

03:28.950 --> 03:30.830
<b>Does this have something to do with Lena?</b>

03:30.830 --> 03:33.250
<b>I’m not sure.
I’m still investigating.</b>

03:33.580 --> 03:36.670
<b>Okay. Let me know if you find out anything!</b>

03:46.140 --> 03:47.680
<b>Shin!</b>

03:48.220 --> 03:49.890
<b>Let’s go water the flowers!</b>

03:50.100 --> 03:52.730
<b>If you could please wait for a bit.
I need to take him on first.</b>

03:52.890 --> 03:56.230
<b>What? But you’re always sparring with Lay!</b>

03:56.440 --> 03:58.820
<b>Even if I water them,
the flowers are only going to dry up.</b>

03:58.980 --> 04:03.070
<b>Why would you say such a thing?
Dummy! You’re a dummy, Shin!</b>

04:03.070 --> 04:04.530
<b>I mean, really...</b>

04:04.530 --> 04:06.530
<b>Want some advice?</b>

04:07.910 --> 04:10.790
<b>Tell her you’ll take care
of me right away for her sake,</b>

04:10.790 --> 04:12.160
<b>and she’ll cheer up.</b>

04:15.080 --> 04:19.710
<b>Leno. For your sake, I will dispatch him
right away, so please be patient for a bit.</b>

04:20.000 --> 04:21.920
<b>Gotcha! I’ll be waiting!</b>

04:22.130 --> 04:25.760
<b>Good luck, Shin! Get him!
You can do it!</b>

04:25.760 --> 04:27.260
<b>I’m quite taken aback.</b>

04:27.260 --> 04:29.310
<b>The important thing is how you tell her.</b>

04:29.310 --> 04:29.970
<b>No.</b>

04:30.640 --> 04:33.100
<b>I’m talking about the rapid strides you’ve made.</b>

04:33.100 --> 04:36.480
<b>That move you just made was one
I only showed you yesterday, was it not?</b>

04:36.770 --> 04:40.070
<b>You’ve been absorbing my sword skills
with each match.</b>

04:40.070 --> 04:42.860
<b>Compared to when we first met,
you’re like a different swordsman.</b>

04:43.190 --> 04:45.700
<b>Well, I think it’s about time that
I gave you back this sword, so—</b>

05:10.640 --> 05:13.270
<b>All right, then.
Allow me to show you.</b>

05:17.900 --> 05:19.480
<b><i>Magic power... disabled?</i></b>

05:39.380 --> 05:41.380
<b>Well, that was a close one.</b>

05:44.300 --> 05:46.720
<b>But why?
I thought you’d blocked that!</b>

05:50.350 --> 05:53.470
<b>Bladeless Sword,
First Hidden Art, Moment.</b>

05:53.970 --> 05:58.600
<b>The blade of the Bladeless Sword, Cadenalios,
does not exist in the present.</b>

05:58.600 --> 06:00.900
<b>Rather, it’s constantly slicing
through moments in the past.</b>

06:01.190 --> 06:03.980
<b>So you slashed me an instant ago, huh?</b>

06:04.530 --> 06:06.820
<b>Is that why you disabled your magic power?</b>

06:07.950 --> 06:10.030
<b>Once it reaches the zone of nothingness,</b>

06:10.030 --> 06:14.540
<b>you can access the sword’s
true hidden power... its Hidden Art.</b>

06:15.290 --> 06:17.830
<b>Did that move work on the Hero Kanon?</b>

06:18.410 --> 06:22.040
<b>Unfortunately, it was only created after I’d lost...</b>

06:22.750 --> 06:26.420
<b>So I’m grateful that you showed
it to me before reincarnating.</b>

06:26.420 --> 06:31.180
<b>If I am reborn,
I may never reach that mystery again.</b>

06:32.640 --> 06:33.890
<b>They’re gonna dry up again!</b>

06:34.010 --> 06:35.680
<b>There’ll be no flowers left!</b>

06:35.680 --> 06:38.060
<b>You think so?
You never know!</b>

06:38.430 --> 06:41.150
<b>I believe the Tithis are right.</b>

06:45.070 --> 06:48.400
<b>What did we tell you?
They dried up!</b>

06:48.400 --> 06:49.530
<b>Why...</b>

06:50.320 --> 06:51.610
<b>...aren’t you scolding me?</b>

06:51.610 --> 06:54.830
<b>Huh? But I was the one who asked you to do it.</b>

06:54.830 --> 06:56.870
<b>You were angry before, though.</b>

06:56.870 --> 06:58.290
<b>Oh, that.</b>

06:58.620 --> 07:00.710
<b>That was my fault, okay?</b>

07:01.000 --> 07:03.330
<b>Because I didn’t know anything about you, Shin.</b>

07:03.330 --> 07:07.550
<b>But it’s different now!
I know you’re doing your best to water them.</b>

07:09.010 --> 07:11.300
<b>I think you’re showering them with love!</b>

07:21.390 --> 07:23.900
<b>Misha, did anything out of the ordinary happen?</b>

07:23.900 --> 07:24.810
<b>It’s the same as always.</b>

07:25.060 --> 07:26.070
<b>You know what?</b>

07:26.070 --> 07:27.280
<b>Let us tell you something!</b>

07:27.280 --> 07:28.690
<b>We saw it the other day!</b>

07:28.690 --> 07:30.450
<b>A headless demon!</b>

07:30.450 --> 07:31.610
<b>Headless?</b>

07:31.820 --> 07:32.910
<b>He was walking through the forest.</b>

07:32.910 --> 07:34.570
<b>So scary!</b>

07:34.570 --> 07:37.450
<b>Must be the Blaze Death King,
whose head got chopped off by Shin.</b>

07:37.450 --> 07:39.040
<b>Where did that demon go?</b>

07:39.040 --> 07:41.410
<b>He left Aharthern.</b>

07:41.410 --> 07:43.620
<b>Hmm. Let’s head over there.</b>

07:48.380 --> 07:51.510
<b>What’s the Blaze Death King up to?</b>

07:51.510 --> 07:53.760
<b>I don’t know.
But according to him,</b>

07:53.760 --> 07:57.560
<b>it’s all so that he can see
me advance even farther.</b>

07:57.560 --> 08:01.270
<b>But if that’s the case, he should stop
searching for enemies and serve me.</b>

08:02.060 --> 08:03.480
<b>A twisted admiration.</b>

08:04.520 --> 08:07.190
<b>What the Blaze Death King is seeing is an idol.</b>

08:07.190 --> 08:11.490
<b>Through the Demon King, he’s gazing
at the object of his admiration in his own head.</b>

08:11.490 --> 08:13.400
<b>He just wants to force his ideals on others.</b>

08:13.400 --> 08:14.200
<b>Hmm.</b>

08:14.740 --> 08:18.910
<b>Meaning that in his eyes,
it doesn’t even have to be me.</b>

08:19.120 --> 08:20.950
<b>As long as he’s as strong as you?</b>

08:20.950 --> 08:22.710
<b>No such person exists.</b>

08:22.710 --> 08:27.210
<b>So in other words, I’m just going
to have to live up to his expectation, eh?</b>

08:28.090 --> 08:32.170
<b>During this era in Delsgade, there
was someone who knew all about the world.</b>

08:32.630 --> 08:34.800
<b>I’m sure that she could locate
the Blaze Death King for me.</b>

08:35.590 --> 08:36.510
<b>Who?</b>

08:36.800 --> 08:38.760
<b><i>The Goddess of Creation Militia.</i></b>

08:38.760 --> 08:41.680
<b><i>She’s the order of creation who made this world,</i></b>

08:41.680 --> 08:43.770
<b><i>and the goddess who built the wall with me.</i></b>

08:44.100 --> 08:47.230
<b>Throughout the last 2,000 years,
she’s been one of my few allies.</b>

08:47.230 --> 08:49.020
<b>So there are good gods, too?</b>

08:49.520 --> 08:51.820
<b>While I do tend to disrupt the divine order,</b>

08:51.820 --> 08:54.110
<b>there’s a handful of gods that I get along with.</b>

08:54.110 --> 08:56.950
<b>Above all, she loved this world.</b>

08:58.240 --> 08:59.870
<b>Please stop!</b>

09:02.080 --> 09:03.330
<b>I knew it.</b>

09:03.750 --> 09:07.290
<b>This kid is seventh in line
to the Azeshion throne... Igareth!</b>

09:07.630 --> 09:08.960
<b>A human child?</b>

09:08.960 --> 09:12.000
<b>He was a hostage,
but I know that I released him.</b>

09:12.340 --> 09:15.220
<b>I thought that he’d gone back
to Gairadite by now.</b>

09:15.930 --> 09:19.510
<b>The Demon King actually let that one go.
What are you going to do?</b>

09:19.510 --> 09:23.180
<b>Our lord is now resting in peace.
I’m sure that he’ll understand.</b>

09:23.720 --> 09:28.600
<b>P-Please, let me go!
All I want is to go home to Azeshion!</b>

09:32.190 --> 09:33.990
<b>My name is Debidora.</b>

09:34.400 --> 09:36.990
<b>This is to avenge my child,
who was murdered by the Hero Jerga.</b>

09:36.990 --> 09:38.410
<b>Pay for it with your life!</b>

09:53.840 --> 09:56.090
<b>Please... spare me...</b>

09:56.300 --> 09:57.550
<b>Did you say, “spare me”?</b>

09:58.180 --> 10:01.260
<b>And how did the human King kill off
the demons who begged for the same thing?</b>

10:01.640 --> 10:03.470
<b>By burning demon children to death,</b>

10:03.470 --> 10:07.810
<b>using their cries of agony to draw demon troops near
so they could massacre them!</b>

10:07.810 --> 10:09.850
<b>Spare... me...</b>

10:10.100 --> 10:12.320
<b>It was you humans who killed them!</b>

10:12.320 --> 10:17.400
<b>So don’t even think about being
so shameless as to beg for your life, human!</b>

10:22.450 --> 10:23.240
<b>Anos...</b>

10:23.240 --> 10:25.240
<b>Even if I were to save him now,</b>

10:25.240 --> 10:29.170
<b>once we’re back 2,000 years in the future,
it’ll revert to the real past.</b>

10:29.170 --> 10:31.210
<b>It’s probably just a fleeting dream.</b>

10:33.340 --> 10:36.170
<b>Now you’re going to suffer
the same agony as my son.</b>

10:36.170 --> 10:40.890
<b>Save me... please... save me!</b>

10:41.640 --> 10:43.930
<b>Demon King!</b>

10:52.440 --> 10:55.570
<b>Not that it will do any good to save you...</b>

10:57.030 --> 11:01.280
<b>But if I don’t at least save him in this dream,
it will be a lie.</b>

11:07.750 --> 11:10.210
<b>Where the hell did you come from?</b>

11:12.750 --> 11:15.500
<b>Lie still for now.
It will be over soon.</b>

11:16.500 --> 11:20.470
<b>Hey, kid, if you’re a fellow demon,
why would you save a human?</b>

11:20.470 --> 11:25.140
<b>That one’s a blood relative of the Hero Jerga,
who mercilessly slaughtered our kind.</b>

11:25.140 --> 11:30.140
<b>Debidora. If he was the one who killed your son,
I’d be fine with you seeking revenge.</b>

11:30.390 --> 11:35.400
<b>But Igareth’s never laid a hand on our brethren,
let alone murdered them.</b>

11:35.650 --> 11:39.490
<b>Has the Demon King Anos granted
you permission to kill the innocent?</b>

11:41.860 --> 11:45.410
<b>Killing innocent children out
of hatred for Azeshion...</b>

11:45.740 --> 11:50.080
<b>...makes you no different than those humans
that you despise so much!</b>

11:50.620 --> 11:52.670
<b>Shut up!</b>

12:10.520 --> 12:11.180
<b>What the—</b>

12:12.560 --> 12:14.310
<b>He’s still on his feet?</b>

12:16.860 --> 12:19.230
<b>Why didn’t you use an Anti-Magic Spell?</b>

12:19.570 --> 12:22.150
<b>I understand your hatred all too well.</b>

12:22.150 --> 12:26.320
<b>I’m sure that the flames
of that hatred are scorching you...</b>

12:26.320 --> 12:28.990
<b>...far more than the small fire
that you just used to burn me.</b>

12:30.620 --> 12:34.000
<b>If you want to hate, then hate.
The right person, that is.</b>

12:34.210 --> 12:36.080
<b>But it’s never going to end.</b>

12:37.420 --> 12:41.590
<b>If you go on hating and killing,
your descendants will be killed again.</b>

12:41.880 --> 12:46.260
<b>Hatred will be passed down to your children eternally,
and then to your grandchildren...</b>

12:46.260 --> 12:48.800
<b>...and will continue to burn Dilhade to a crisp.</b>

12:49.180 --> 12:51.600
<b>I can’t be like the Demon King.</b>

12:52.430 --> 12:55.100
<b>I don’t care if it means that I fall from grace!</b>

12:55.270 --> 13:00.690
<b>I just hate humans, no matter what!</b>

13:15.660 --> 13:19.130
<b>Those eyes... so you’re still alive, then?</b>

13:19.130 --> 13:24.470
<b>What do you mean? I’m Anoshu Polticoal,
a traveling entertainer who’s passing through.</b>

13:26.180 --> 13:29.470
<b>The Demon King was fond of traveling entertainers.</b>

13:31.430 --> 13:33.270
<b>My lord in all your glory...</b>

13:33.470 --> 13:34.930
<b>What you commanded us to do...</b>

13:35.390 --> 13:40.980
<b>We just couldn’t...
we just couldn’t carry it out!</b>

13:41.270 --> 13:44.990
<b>We can’t do it!
We can never forget the hatred we feel.</b>

13:44.990 --> 13:47.950
<b>The humans who murdered our comrades
are on the other side of that wall...</b>

13:47.950 --> 13:50.700
<b>Laughing without a care in the world,
living their lives... they’re alive.</b>

13:50.870 --> 13:54.660
<b>How can we possibly look the other way?</b>

13:57.920 --> 14:00.540
<b>It can be the least possible contradiction.</b>

14:01.630 --> 14:03.090
<b>Look up now.</b>

14:04.210 --> 14:06.470
<b>I have a message
from the Demon King of Tyranny.</b>

14:07.260 --> 14:08.930
<b>“Let us meet again 2,000 years from now.”</b>

14:09.390 --> 14:13.350
<b>A wonderful world awaits you all there.</b>

14:28.860 --> 14:30.570
<b>I knew that you’d save him.</b>

14:30.950 --> 14:32.410
<b>I’m sure it won’t be for nothing.</b>

14:32.410 --> 14:33.330
<b>You’re right.</b>

14:34.410 --> 14:37.120
<b>It may really not have been for nothing.</b>

14:47.970 --> 14:50.760
<b>Venuzdnor... has activated?</b>

14:50.760 --> 14:54.050
<b>There’s no one in this era able to wield
the Magic Sword of Destruction.</b>

14:54.640 --> 14:59.230
<b>Since I’d already reincarnated myself,
and Avos Dilhevia has yet to be born.</b>

14:59.810 --> 15:01.310
<b>I don’t know how it was done,</b>

15:01.650 --> 15:06.360
<b>but someone from this era predicted that I’d
be coming from 2,000 years in the future.</b>

15:06.820 --> 15:10.200
<b>But that could be our salvation.</b>

15:16.580 --> 15:19.830
<b>Normally, the moment I tried to draw it,</b>

15:19.830 --> 15:22.880
<b>the order of time would be activated,
and Revalon would end.</b>

15:23.250 --> 15:27.340
<b>But if Venuzdnor has already shown up
in this past, it’s a different story.</b>

15:28.130 --> 15:33.300
<b>If I can take up Venuzdnor in my hands,
then I can change the past.</b>

15:35.550 --> 15:38.770
<b>Demon King... Demon King!</b>

15:39.390 --> 15:40.850
<b>Demon King!</b>

15:41.140 --> 15:45.020
<b>As the third unit of the Subjugation Battalion
was retreating to Azeshion,</b>

15:45.020 --> 15:46.860
<b>it came under attack by monsters,</b>

15:46.860 --> 15:49.280
<b>and was wiped out so that I could escape.</b>

15:49.280 --> 15:52.070
<b>I got here on my own.</b>

15:53.450 --> 15:55.200
<b>I’m glad that you made it.</b>

15:57.330 --> 15:59.200
<b>Those monsters... were they demons?</b>

15:59.410 --> 16:03.290
<b>No. I’d never seen their kind before.
They looked like this.</b>

16:03.290 --> 16:03.960
<b>Were they dragons?</b>

16:04.120 --> 16:05.290
<b>Dragons?</b>

16:05.290 --> 16:08.000
<b>They’re a rare species
that almost never appears.</b>

16:08.000 --> 16:10.460
<b>I thought that they’d died out long ago.</b>

16:12.010 --> 16:13.090
<b>Igareth.</b>

16:13.880 --> 16:17.600
<b>I’ve returned here from 2,000 years in the future.</b>

16:19.060 --> 16:20.430
<b>You don’t believe me?</b>

16:20.890 --> 16:23.310
<b>No, I do believe you.</b>

16:23.730 --> 16:27.270
<b>But you haven’t been truly saved just yet.</b>

16:27.900 --> 16:33.530
<b>In order to save you, I’d have to kill you once,
then resurrect you again to this point in time.</b>

16:35.450 --> 16:37.950
<b>When you’ve been reborn thanks
to the Magic Sword of Destruction,</b>

16:37.950 --> 16:41.370
<b>you’ll have become an entity that even
the gods of Time can’t detect.</b>

16:42.040 --> 16:43.580
<b>You’re not afraid, are you?</b>

16:43.580 --> 16:45.870
<b>Is there something that I can do?</b>

16:46.540 --> 16:51.090
<b>Because I was taught that a Hero
must repay the one he owes his life to.</b>

16:51.670 --> 16:56.050
<b>Then when you’re reborn,
I want you to spread a certain rumor.</b>

16:56.050 --> 17:01.220
<b>A rumor about the Demon King of Tyranny,
Avos Dilhevia, that will endure 2,000 years from now.</b>

17:01.220 --> 17:03.810
<b>I’m going to imprint it on your memory
so you won’t forget.</b>

17:04.980 --> 17:08.440
<b>A rumor that you’ve spread after transforming
into a unique existence...</b>

17:08.440 --> 17:11.360
<b>...should never fade away,
and still be intact until the present.</b>

17:17.530 --> 17:20.740
<b>Igareth. You proud little Hero...</b>

17:21.790 --> 17:25.710
<b>I want you to save the other Demon King,
the bearer of a sad fate.</b>

17:26.000 --> 17:30.420
<b>I, Igareth, promise to live up
to your expectations, Demon King!</b>

17:32.210 --> 17:33.300
<b>Let us meet again.</b>

17:39.930 --> 17:41.350
<b>Venuzdnor...</b>

17:41.350 --> 17:44.350
<b>Looks like it’s run out of Delsgade’s magic.</b>

17:45.020 --> 17:46.230
<b>Anos?</b>

17:50.560 --> 17:54.030
<b>“To my Demon King.
Let us meet again 2,000 years from now.”</b>

17:54.030 --> 17:55.530
<b>“The three of us, next time.”</b>

17:55.530 --> 17:58.030
<b>“Surely... definitely... no matter what.”</b>

17:58.030 --> 18:00.320
<b>“I shall fall in love once again.”</b>

18:01.620 --> 18:02.450
<b>Love...</b>

18:03.200 --> 18:06.120
<b>Who would’ve thought this would happen
in the Mythical Age?</b>

18:06.120 --> 18:08.250
<b>You mean no one ever fell in love?</b>

18:08.250 --> 18:12.380
<b>Even if one had such feelings,
it wasn’t peaceful enough to express them.</b>

18:13.550 --> 18:16.470
<b>Whoever wrote this must’ve been
in that situation.</b>

18:17.420 --> 18:18.510
<b>Is something wrong?</b>

18:18.510 --> 18:20.390
<b>It’s under a spell.</b>

18:21.640 --> 18:22.720
<b>I see.</b>

18:23.180 --> 18:25.680
<b>We may have to wait until night.</b>

18:29.060 --> 18:32.150
<b>All you ever do is hang out with Lay!
Really, now!</b>

18:32.150 --> 18:34.730
<b>I see that Shin’s at her beck and call, as usual.</b>

18:34.730 --> 18:37.190
<b>Can Shin ever find love?</b>

18:37.190 --> 18:40.360
<b>If it’s something that he wants with all his heart,
it should be possible.</b>

18:40.360 --> 18:43.530
<b>His source is a Magic Sword.
Will it still be all right?</b>

18:43.950 --> 18:47.250
<b>Just because he’s a Magic Sword,
did you think he couldn’t love anyone?</b>

18:48.500 --> 18:51.790
<b>A world where you can never gain
your heart’s desires...</b>

18:51.790 --> 18:54.090
<b>...should be wiped off the face of the earth.</b>

18:54.090 --> 18:56.670
<b>The Goddess of Creation Militia
was known to say that.</b>

18:56.670 --> 18:58.420
<b>What kind of god was she?</b>

18:58.420 --> 19:00.720
<b>A kind-hearted, heroic god.</b>

19:01.180 --> 19:06.350
<b>Most gods never pay any attention
to the Demons and humans who live in this world.</b>

19:06.350 --> 19:10.440
<b>That’s what leads to all kinds of injustice,
and widespread tragedy.</b>

19:13.150 --> 19:17.530
<b>But the world’s spiritual essence
is overflowing with her affection.</b>

19:17.530 --> 19:21.110
<b>If you desire it with all your heart,
she’s sure to come through for you.</b>

19:21.110 --> 19:22.490
<b>Do you believe that?</b>

19:22.490 --> 19:24.280
<b>Militia was quite distressed.</b>

19:24.280 --> 19:26.950
<b>“I’ve created a sad world,” she said.</b>

19:26.950 --> 19:29.330
<b>And so I made her a certain promise.</b>

19:29.710 --> 19:31.080
<b>What kind of promise?</b>

19:31.460 --> 19:35.290
<b>That if the gods were causing
hopeless tragedies and injustices,</b>

19:35.710 --> 19:38.130
<b>then I would destroy them.</b>

19:38.590 --> 19:41.180
<b>I wanted to make sure that Militia knew.</b>

19:41.180 --> 19:45.640
<b>That this world that she’d created wouldn’t succumb
to something like injustice.</b>

19:48.270 --> 19:49.350
<b>Anos?</b>

19:49.640 --> 19:50.480
<b>What is it?</b>

19:50.930 --> 19:53.150
<b>Did the world become a peaceful place?</b>

19:53.150 --> 19:54.560
<b>More than before, yes.</b>

19:54.860 --> 19:57.150
<b>But it seems like we’re not quite there yet.</b>

19:59.820 --> 20:01.320
<b>“To the Demon King, Anos.”</b>

20:01.650 --> 20:06.070
<b>“The Blaze Death King is in the cemetery
which honors the war dead.”</b>

20:06.070 --> 20:09.490
<b>“Also... I hope that the future
of the kind-hearted Demon King,”</b>

20:09.750 --> 20:11.870
<b>“who fought to the point that he
was known as a tyrant,”</b>

20:12.160 --> 20:14.670
<b>“will be filled with peace.”</b>

20:14.670 --> 20:18.090
<b>“I will always be nearby,
watching over you.”</b>

20:18.090 --> 20:20.460
<b>“Until I draw my last breath... forever.”</b>

20:21.300 --> 20:26.140
<b>I don’t understand. You couldn’t write these words
unless you knew that you were coming here.</b>

20:26.140 --> 20:29.560
<b>It must be Militia.
She has her eye on the world.</b>

20:29.560 --> 20:30.810
<b>On Venuzdnor, too?</b>

20:30.810 --> 20:35.150
<b>Could be. Though I don’t think
she’s capable of wielding it.</b>

20:35.440 --> 20:37.770
<b>The Goddess of Creation isn’t here?</b>

20:37.770 --> 20:39.650
<b>- No.
- Are you sad?</b>

20:39.650 --> 20:42.990
<b>It would’ve been nice to have seen
an old friend, of course.</b>

20:42.990 --> 20:45.660
<b>But the souvenir she’s left me
is more than enough.</b>

20:47.410 --> 20:49.160
<b>I’d like to make a stop somewhere.</b>

20:53.870 --> 20:54.830
<b>The cemetery?</b>

20:54.830 --> 20:55.830
<b>That’s right.</b>

20:56.170 --> 20:57.500
<b>Do you see it, Misha?</b>

20:58.670 --> 21:01.840
<b>All these people...
I couldn’t protect them.</b>

21:02.760 --> 21:07.720
<b>They were drawn to my dream of peace,
and fought for me until they were wiped out.</b>

21:07.720 --> 21:10.760
<b>The more loyal they were,
the sooner they perished.</b>

21:11.520 --> 21:15.980
<b>I had to become stronger so
that I could live up to their hopes.</b>

21:16.350 --> 21:20.360
<b>Even if that meant being called a tyrant,
or having to do cruel things.</b>

21:20.770 --> 21:23.940
<b>And then I reigned over this land
as the Demon King.</b>

21:23.940 --> 21:28.990
<b>But no matter how much power I gain,
I’ll never regain the lives of those I’ve lost.</b>

21:30.530 --> 21:32.330
<b>I have good news for you all.</b>

21:32.700 --> 21:36.870
<b>We’ve achieved peace. You should be proud.
We’ve won, you see.</b>

21:40.920 --> 21:45.920
<b>I would’ve liked to have gazed upon
that tranquil town with you all from here.</b>

21:46.090 --> 21:47.550
<b>White Flower.</b>

22:00.230 --> 22:01.650
<b>Smile for them.</b>

22:04.440 --> 22:09.740
<b>They wanted to see how their lord
would smile in a peaceful era.</b>

22:10.070 --> 22:11.330
<b>What makes you say that?</b>

22:11.580 --> 22:14.790
<b>It feels as though everyone’s emotions
are still here.</b>

22:16.080 --> 22:18.710
<b>Their souls are with you, Anos.</b>

22:20.210 --> 22:25.300
<b>It was thanks to all your help that I
was able to go to a peaceful era.</b>

22:26.510 --> 22:27.510
<b>Thank you.</b>

22:29.720 --> 22:32.050
<b>I’ll see to it that it wasn’t in vain.</b>

23:35.610 --> 23:39.990
<b>A PRAYER FOR TWO THOUSAND YEARS LATER</b>

23:37.290 --> 23:39.540
<b><i>A Prayer for Two Thousand Years Later</i></b>
